From 56a03e30d4058b164ed8ddd216f0311100fc7857 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephenuffugus <99242197+Stephenuffugus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 20:57:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Make Trackfit free: remove the paid tier and photo
 identification
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner's decision — it becomes another free app in the Sky Wolf Studio
portfolio. "Take out any photo IDing and stuff and just let people put in all
the different pieces they have and it formulate what builds they can do."

Removed the paid tier: premium.ts, PremiumGate, PremiumModal,
LicenseActivation, PremiumPricingTest, pricing-feedback, every VITE_PREMIUM_*
var and the Payhip links. Everything a Founder could do, everyone can now do —
the inventory PDF and all eight vendor listings are simply available.

Removed photo identification, which is the part that should not have shipped
at all. It was never real: both proxy env vars were empty in production, so
every user got buildStubCandidates() — invented pieces with hardcoded
confidences [0.95, 0.72, 0.55] against an auto-fill threshold of 0.85. Top-1
always cleared it, so the stub silently wrote a made-up piece into the user's
inventory. The result carried fromStub: true and nothing in the app ever read
it, so nobody was told. It was also the headline unlock behind a $19 gate.
Gone with it: the Supabase edge function, the Cloudflare worker, and the CI
secrets that fed them.

Removed the affiliate_tag plumbing from packages/marketplace so it cannot be
switched on by accident.

Verified green, not assumed:
  pnpm -r run typecheck          pass
  pnpm -r test                   84 passed, 1 skipped
  VITE_BASE_PATH=/trackfit/ build  16 precache entries, 1027 KiB

And the one that matters most: `grep -rn "fetch(" apps/web/src packages/*/src`
now returns nothing. There is no code path left that talks to a server, which
is what makes "nothing leaves your device" literally true rather than nearly
true.

Two things this commit does NOT do, deliberately:

  · 25 Founder licence hashes were issued for Payhip auto-delivery on
    2026-05-29. Anyone who paid now gets everything free, which is fine, but
    they may be owed a note. That is the owner's call.
  · The layout suggester is still a feasibility scorecard rather than a
    planner, and "Build this" is still a button with no handler. Separate
    problems, separately fixed.
